 {:seon.task/name "a-docs-edit-is-proved-by-its-readers-in-seconds"
  :seon.task/plan "Measured 2026-11-14: a fresh agent's (my.agent/prove) of one docs/prompt.md edit ran 17+ minutes without answering, root at ~1 core meanwhile, and root's REPL queued behind it. Owner: \"the test suite is supposed to be a handful of minutes worst case\". Find the cause first (hypothesis: the edit reaches ~104 doc-reader tests plus deferred process tests, cold after every digest moved). Then a run selects only the tests whose recorded reads include the changed section, and a run that cannot finish answers a typed error, never hangs. Owners: tests, data. Cause measured 2026-11-15 [M, tests-4: bin/test --plan both --merge digests at 1aaeb145f6 before and after a one-line docs/decisions.md edit, reverted]: 88 tests and 3 steps (health, laws, test-inputs) move. 9 take the wiki class ([:config :seon.env/docs]); 78 take [:tree], the whole checkout, because a test form's raw read (seon.program/tree-readers: slurp, file-seq, io/resource) of one checkout file puts it on the whole tree (seon.program/checkout-read?, :scans): seon.ctx.wire-test's 30 slurp only (str (seon.config/checkout) \"/\" seon.doc/system-page). So any edit anywhere, src included, reruns those 78; 49 of them run no process. A green's recorded :reads keep [:tree] and the class whole (target/results/<test>/reads.edn), never the files read. The fix (90/10, what exists: seon.proofs/reads-key already takes :files, seon.program/reads-index holds each [:file path] blob, seon.proofs/read-digests reuses by them): a test's run records the checkout files it opened (relative paths, through the one measured run seon.proofs uses for both runners, a shard's and an agent's test child), and a green whose test reaches no process or binary keeps those [:file p] in its :reads in place of [:tree]; a test reaching a process keeps [:tree] (what it reads is out of this process's sight). Estimate: one conj per file a test opens; a docs edit then reruns the 9 class readers, the 29 [:tree] tests that run a process, and the tests that opened that page, against 88; an src edit stops rerunning the 49. The proof is measured on the same edit."
