e's unnamed print site seon.system/flow-report [M]: the test reads every form through test-runner/program, but its digest takes only what it calls, so trees whose programs differ share it. The class: a test reading all forms keyed by only what it calls; its cure is recorded reads (docs/plan.md item 4, context's core), never a digest of the whole tree (owner: \"no test digests the whole tree\"); this is its first case (root). (5) seon.check-test/the-health-step-reads-a-base-whose-alias-the-head-retargets, red in deps' (16:11) and runtime's (16:18) land proves, green alone: the base checkout's runner planned another tree than its commit's, so a file appeared in a fresh checkout under concurrent runs [H]; make-base-tree!'s error now names the checkout's files off its commit (jolt/tests), the evidence the next red gives. Last of (4): step-bounds, bin/bounded, bin/stalls, bin/check's watchdog and arm-wall! each become that one bound (root's list) and are deleted, each named with what does its job."
